Sophgo SG200x (cv181x) vendor drivers, imported in-tree
======================================================

Provenance
----------

  osdrv/  sophgo/osdrv @ f35ca075cc022aac97f5d22238c1e46caf8276bd, interdrv/
          (GPL-2.0). Includes include/, cif, vi, vpss, vo, fb, ive, dwa,
          rgn, mon, snsr_i2c, sys, base, tpu, vcodec, jpeg, cvi_vc_drv,
          rtos_cmdqu, fast_image, wiegand, clock_cooling, plus the vendor
          pinctrl headers (kernel-5.10-headers/, GPL-2.0) which cif and vo
          include.

          The Linux 7.2 port of sys/base/snsr_i2c/cif/vi/vpss/vcodec/
          jpeg/cvi_vc_drv/tpu was taken from djairjr/recamera-linux-kernel7
          @ 240adcc6164d7ff50995c0119f29a1ba570ea57d,
          external/package/sophgo-osdrv/000{1,2,3}-*.patch and is already
          applied to the files here (marked "7.2 port"), not at build time.
          The other modules were ported the same way: void platform remove,
          one-argument class_create, pde_data, the gpiod descriptor API, the
          5-argument thermal_of_cooling_device_register, the descriptor
          IRQ-less probe paths and the DMA-buf namespace. That is the
          compile baseline; 7.3.3-specific fixes are marked "7.3".

  ion/    The vendor ION allocator: sophgo/linux_5.10 @ d0486a96,
          drivers/staging/android/ion (GPL-2.0), with the cvitek carveout
          heap and /dev/ion glue, 7.2/7.3 ported in place (no build-time
          patch). CONFIG_ION, CONFIG_ION_CVITEK and
          CONFIG_ION_CARVEOUT_HEAP are defined once for this directory and
          all of osdrv/ by the subdir-ccflags-y in Makefile: they change
          struct ion_buffer, so ion.ko and every osdrv module must see the
          same values.

Vendor modules superseded by mainline drivers (not imported)
------------------------------------------------------------

  rtc/   -> drivers/rtc/rtc-cv1800.c                        (sophgo,cv1800b-rtc)
  saradc/-> drivers/iio/adc/sophgo-cv1800b-adc.c            (sophgo,cv1800b-saradc)
  pwm/   -> drivers/pwm/pwm-cv1800.c                        (sophgo,cv1800-pwm)
  wdt/   -> drivers/watchdog/dw_wdt.c + sophgo,cv1800-wdt   (chip reset bits)

Device tree
-----------

  Multimedia nodes: arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2002-multimedia.dtsi
  Board:            arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2002-licheerv-nano-b.dts

  The nodes keep the vendor compatibles and the clock/reset/reg/interrupt
  names the drivers request; the interrupt numbers are the vendor PLIC
  numbers converted with SOC_PERIPHERAL_IRQ(). The DT bindings in
  Documentation/devicetree/bindings are only written for the drivers that
  were brought to mainline style (pwm, thermal, restart, dw-wdt); the
  staging drivers keep the vendor ABI documented by this file.

Userspace and firmware dependencies (not kernel side)
-----------------------------------------------------

  * sophgo/cvi_mpi @ 6dbbbb8bed877cd3a08f76ce4aed61645c38bbe1 -- the MPI
    library the applications link against (ion_fd based). Without it the
    /dev/cvi-* nodes are unusable.
  * cviruntime @ 3f4938648950a7f3bf9a19c320ca9fae7c52de20, cvikernel @
    9f1f57a19c3c281a931dfc71b318494487193d56, cvibuilder @
    4309f2a649fc7cfe7160389d52a81c469dbdd7bc -- NPU model runtime.
  * sophgo/ramdisk @ f855ea377c886aae094e224f4dffebcffaedc4ad
    usr/share/fw_vcodec/{coda980.bin,monet.bin} -- codec MCU firmware read
    by cvi_vc_driver when the first H.264/H.265 channel is created.
  * 3A/ISP tuning bins and the sensor drivers live in the sensor support
    list and in the MPI (SensorSupportList @
    86b0708e0101dfd4b60abafe98fef28c92773dbb), not in the kernel.
  * CV_MPI needs the fip's pinmux (the Sipeed U-Boot sets the display,
    touch, camera and SDIO pads), and the C906L FreeRTOS image for
    rtos_cmdqu/fast_image.
  * C906 + fence.tso: userspace must be built with -mno-fence-tso or against
    an OpenSBI >= 1.7, else any __atomic_thread_fence(ACQ_REL) SIGILLs.

Clocks, resets and MMIO (audited for 7.3)
----------------------------------------

  * The VIP/SC register bank is shared by vi, vpss, dwa, vo, fb and ive.
    vpss now enables CLK_SRC_VIP_SYS_1 and CLK_SC_TOP_VIP before its first
    register access and holds them while bound; vo/fb reach the same bank
    through vpss callbacks and must not be probed before vpss (the Makefile
    and Kconfig order guarantees this).
  * vo owns only CLK_DISP_VIP (plus CLK_DSI_MAC_VIP/CLK_BT_VIP for the
    matching interfaces); the dead clk_sc_top member and the swapped
    enable/disable pair in vo_release() were removed.
  * dwa clocks CLK_DWA_VIP around the probe-time interrupt-mask write; the
    per-job path keeps enabling/disabling it.
  * ive needs CLK_IVE_VIP before any register access: the node MUST provide
    clocks = <&clk CLK_IVE_VIP>; clock-names = "clk_ive"; (the driver now
    fails probe without it). The sg2002-multimedia.dtsi ive node does not
    have it yet.
  * jpeg/vcodec keep their vendor "clock gating disabled" policy
    (VCODEC_MASK_DISABLE_CLK_GATING path), but only after enabling the gate
    before the first register write.
  * rtos_cmdqu (C906 mailbox) and mon (DDR/AXI monitor) have no CCF gate in
    clk-cv1800, so they need no clock reference.
  * cvifb publishes the non-coherent framebuffer with
    dma_sync_single_for_device() instead of the unexported
    arch_sync_dma_for_device().

Not yet ported / owned elsewhere
--------------------------------

  * Hynitron touch (vendor hyn_ts, "hyn,7xx"): ported by HynitronPort, not
    here. The GT911 panels work through drivers/input/touchscreen/goodix.c.
  * The vendor dwc2 fork interface /proc/cviusb/otg_role and the
    "cvitek,wifi-pin"/"cvitek,bt-pin" power-sequencing drivers are not
    ported; the USB role is set through the DT dr_mode, and the wireless
    power sequence is done by the fip.
  * rtl8733bs: GPL-2.0 source exists (briansune/rtl8733BS_WiFi_linux and
    other vendor drops) and is being ported by Rtl8733Port; it is not part
    of this directory. AIC8800 (deepin-community/aic8800) is the other
    LicheeRV Nano wireless variant.
  * Board DTS (B/E/W/WE) is owned by LicheeBoardCoverage.
